WEBVTT

00:02.980 --> 00:06.630
Transfer location coordinates set.

00:06.630 --> 00:08.140
Transfer in ten seconds.

00:08.140 --> 00:10.230
Director Yamato is returning.

00:10.230 --> 00:14.540
More accurately, it's the witch's 
apprentice disguised as Yamato.

00:14.540 --> 00:17.360
I'll avenge you, Yamato.

00:19.780 --> 00:23.870
Transfer complete in three, two, one...

00:23.870 --> 00:24.620
Fire.

00:34.340 --> 00:35.140
What?

00:35.140 --> 00:38.790
A-Additional commands were issued 
to the transfer system.

00:38.790 --> 00:41.010
The transfer coordinates were changed.

00:41.010 --> 00:42.770
Where is he? Find him immediately.

00:42.770 --> 00:44.260
His device isn't responding.

00:44.260 --> 00:45.720
I can't trace him.

00:57.860 --> 01:03.490
You win this round, witch's apprentice.

03:02.410 --> 03:04.010
Look.

03:04.460 --> 03:06.570
It's the Southern Triple Cross.

03:07.730 --> 03:10.030
We're back on the planet's surface.

03:12.020 --> 03:13.630
The surface...

03:18.370 --> 03:23.290
We'll begin our conquest of Redia by doing
whatever we can. Start small, as they say.

03:28.570 --> 03:31.060
Wait, Adonis. They're still there.

03:31.060 --> 03:34.060
There are witches who are still alive.

03:34.830 --> 03:37.050
Hear me, system.

03:37.050 --> 03:39.800
Change transfer coordinates.

03:40.310 --> 03:43.940
Planet's surface, coordinates 37N-42.

03:43.950 --> 03:48.450
<b>Voice 
Authenticated</b>

03:44.320 --> 03:48.450
<i>Change accepted, authorized 
user Director Yamato.</i>

03:59.360 --> 04:03.740
We'll attack cities and villages on our way 
to Redia in the northern hemisphere.

04:03.740 --> 04:08.340
We'll procure information 
and supplies as we prepare ourselves.

04:08.770 --> 04:10.470
I'd like medicine, too.

04:15.140 --> 04:18.100
I want to go back to the others.

04:19.360 --> 04:21.260
You must be stupid.

04:21.260 --> 04:24.850
There's no way any of the
witches on the moon survived.

04:24.850 --> 04:26.980
That's not true.

04:26.980 --> 04:28.470
Send me back.

04:28.470 --> 04:30.230
What are you, a spoiled child?

04:30.470 --> 04:32.400
Are you talking about yourself?

04:32.400 --> 04:35.220
All you care about is revenge.

04:37.240 --> 04:41.270
Written-Style Summoning Magic: 
Nostalgic Memories.

04:42.960 --> 04:49.250
Promise me you won't attack us or Adonis.

04:49.250 --> 04:53.000
Promise me this, and I'll dispel my magic.

04:53.280 --> 04:55.500
Let's shake hands and make up.

04:55.840 --> 04:57.260
Don't.

04:57.760 --> 05:01.930
I see now why you didn't 
fit in with the other witches.

05:01.930 --> 05:05.710
You must be out of your mind 
to want to reconcile with humans.

05:08.270 --> 05:11.260
I always wanted to meet you.

05:11.260 --> 05:15.780
I wanted to know what kind of person 
Chloe had chosen as her apprentice.

05:15.780 --> 05:20.780
I was dying to know what 
kind of person Adonis was.

05:21.330 --> 05:23.960
Despite being a human, 
he was a witch's apprentice.

05:23.960 --> 05:26.790
Living between two worlds,

05:27.180 --> 05:31.530
I believed you could become 
a bridge between humans and witches.

05:32.100 --> 05:36.540
You were my hope.

05:37.760 --> 05:39.050
See?

05:39.900 --> 05:42.060
You understand nothing about me.

05:42.300 --> 05:45.260
Then how far will you go?

05:45.260 --> 05:47.810
I know you sensed it during 
the battle on the moon.

05:48.170 --> 05:53.560
Just as you hate humankind, 
they'll never forgive you.

05:53.860 --> 05:56.960
The fighting will never stop.

05:56.960 --> 06:00.560
If someone doesn't end it, 
hate will never be erased from our world—

06:00.560 --> 06:03.070
Your words mean nothing to me.

06:04.720 --> 06:08.770
Chloe's life is more precious 
than all of humanity.

06:08.770 --> 06:12.350
The world that took her from me
 deserves to be destroyed.

06:13.540 --> 06:15.550
And what will you sacrifice to achieve that?

06:16.340 --> 06:19.940
What happened to the witches 
because of your rage?

06:19.940 --> 06:22.340
Because you summoned the humans there...

06:22.340 --> 06:25.970
We're back on the surface 
because I summoned them.

06:28.350 --> 06:31.730
Your friends served as a useful smokescreen.

06:32.080 --> 06:33.760
How could you?

06:35.010 --> 06:37.230
How could you say that?

06:39.530 --> 06:42.390
They did everything they could 
to survive the witch hunts!

06:42.390 --> 06:46.500
How dare you belittle 
their lives—belittle us!

06:46.500 --> 06:48.740
Who's belittling who?

06:48.740 --> 06:51.360
You keep blathering on and on,

06:51.360 --> 06:54.380
but haven't you witnessed 
countless friends die?

06:54.380 --> 06:56.840
And yet you want to forgive the humans?

06:56.840 --> 07:00.500
You're the one committing the greatest 
offense against your friends' lives!

07:02.270 --> 07:03.730
But...

07:05.260 --> 07:09.020
Revenge won't heal your wounds.

07:09.020 --> 07:10.510
I don't care.

07:10.970 --> 07:13.860
I don't have anything left to lose.

07:27.140 --> 07:29.840
You still have the life Chloe protected.

07:30.410 --> 07:35.640
No matter how cruel, hollow, 
or cold this world is,

07:36.260 --> 07:38.790
don't let that change you.

07:40.310 --> 07:43.640
I won't tell you to forgive them 
for what they've done.

07:43.640 --> 07:47.810
But if you continue with your revenge, 
it will shatter your heart.

07:48.560 --> 07:52.510
You'll end up like the humans 
who took Chloe from you.

07:53.990 --> 07:58.070
You still have plenty to lose.

08:02.900 --> 08:05.910
You don't get it.

08:06.650 --> 08:09.180
Revenge is proof of my existence.

08:10.140 --> 08:15.090
Irreplaceable proof 
that Chloe lived with me.

08:16.100 --> 08:21.480
I feel like all traces of Chloe's existence 
would vanish if I stopped seeking revenge.

08:22.370 --> 08:24.100
I'm scared.

08:24.980 --> 08:27.340
Do you understand that?

08:32.900 --> 08:35.850
All you do is cry.

08:36.770 --> 08:39.340
I know. I'm sorry.

08:39.340 --> 08:40.610
I...

08:46.280 --> 08:47.640
Adonis?

08:49.030 --> 08:51.260
Look at the hot couple.

08:51.260 --> 08:54.500
Let's see... Here's your update.

08:54.500 --> 09:00.060
I see a couple engaging in a passionate 
embrace under the moon at 12 o'clock.

09:00.460 --> 09:04.090
I'm amazed they're going at it
 in the middle of this desert.

09:04.090 --> 09:06.530
Think they're slaves 
who escaped from the city?

09:06.530 --> 09:08.460
They both look too decent for that.

09:08.460 --> 09:11.350
They're probably just 
a couple of kids who eloped.

09:11.350 --> 09:13.900
What a pain in the ass.

09:13.900 --> 09:16.260
No amount of stupidity surprises me anymore.

09:16.260 --> 09:18.480
We're not living in the old world anymore.

09:19.340 --> 09:22.580
So, what should we do, Mr. Punch?

09:23.400 --> 09:26.990
Resident of the Wastelands
Ringleader Punch

09:43.640 --> 09:49.000
I've had enough of waking up 
in places I don't recognize.

09:50.110 --> 09:55.250
I lost consciousness, and then...

10:02.740 --> 10:06.390
Excuse me. Please help us.

10:06.390 --> 10:08.670
My friend is hurt.

10:11.870 --> 10:15.790
We're lost.

10:18.490 --> 10:22.350
Which means we're at those bikers' hideout.

10:22.350 --> 10:24.430
You're awake, kid?

10:26.730 --> 10:30.440
Look at those eyes. Have you killed someone?

10:33.570 --> 10:35.540
Have a drink.

10:35.540 --> 10:37.580
Nothing helps you get over an injury better.

10:40.080 --> 10:41.580
<i>So he's a vagrant.</i>

10:41.580 --> 10:44.840
I'm not into sipping on sewer water.

10:46.720 --> 10:48.640
Now that's funny.

10:48.640 --> 10:52.710
Calling humanity's greatest 
invention sewer water?

10:56.750 --> 11:00.100
I'm Punch. I run this place.

11:00.590 --> 11:03.170
<i>Is "this place" a settlement after all?</i>

11:03.170 --> 11:05.610
<i>It doesn't seem to be under Redia's control.</i>

11:06.490 --> 11:09.170
I was with a young woman.

11:09.170 --> 11:10.330
Where is she?

11:11.190 --> 11:15.120
The pink-haired girl? She's a cutie.

11:15.120 --> 11:17.470
Is she your girlfriend?

11:17.470 --> 11:19.980
She was taking care of you 
until a moment ago.

11:19.980 --> 11:23.610
Some of our youngsters dragged her off.

11:23.610 --> 11:25.250
Answer the question.

11:25.730 --> 11:27.250
What have you done with her?

11:28.570 --> 11:31.000
Don't be so angry.

11:32.010 --> 11:34.630
Come with me, kid.

11:44.140 --> 11:46.220
The wastelands.

11:46.220 --> 11:51.770
The other side of 
the super-industrial revolution.

11:51.770 --> 11:57.160
People from developing countries, refugees, 
and slaves who have escaped from Redia.

11:57.160 --> 12:03.790
Everyone left behind by science 
ends up here and becomes a vagrant.

12:06.930 --> 12:08.290
Sounds miserable.

12:08.290 --> 12:09.550
Right?

12:09.550 --> 12:11.040
No! Stop!

12:14.960 --> 12:17.210
Please stop!

12:17.210 --> 12:19.540
I can't do it!

12:20.720 --> 12:23.490
No! Stop!

12:25.850 --> 12:27.230
What are they doing to her?

12:27.230 --> 12:32.350
We don't get many women around here, 
especially not young ones.

12:32.350 --> 12:36.510
Your girlfriend's <i>real</i> good at screaming.

12:43.940 --> 12:45.430
Scum.

12:51.750 --> 12:55.680
I can't! I'm going to fall!

12:51.750 --> 12:56.500
<b><i>VROOM</i></b>

12:56.500 --> 12:58.620
How do you ride this thing?

12:56.500 --> 13:02.390
<i><b>SPIN SPIN SPIN</b></i>

12:58.620 --> 13:02.390
Someone make it stop!

13:02.630 --> 13:04.520
That's it, girlie!

13:02.640 --> 13:06.120
Raise your hips and 
use your knees as a cushion!

13:06.730 --> 13:08.930
What an awesome show!

13:09.390 --> 13:11.520
<i><b>SPIN SPIN SPIN</b></i>

13:09.780 --> 13:11.870
What are you doing?

13:11.520 --> 13:12.400
<i><b>SCREECH</b></i>

13:12.650 --> 13:15.910
Adonis, you're awake. I'm so glad.

13:20.950 --> 13:22.790
Have your injuries healed?

13:22.790 --> 13:24.030
I'm more worried about yours.

13:24.030 --> 13:27.030
Oh, right. These are for you.

13:27.040 --> 13:32.040
Symbol of

13:27.040 --> 13:32.040
Reconciliation

13:27.830 --> 13:31.650
I'm sorry I didn't realize you were injured.

13:32.030 --> 13:35.790
And for all the cruel things I said.

13:38.310 --> 13:39.780
What are these? I don't want them.

13:39.780 --> 13:41.050
What?!

13:41.330 --> 13:43.310
Hey, boys.

13:43.310 --> 13:46.050
We're throwing a party. Get set up.

13:46.050 --> 13:48.560
Yeah!

13:46.340 --> 13:48.550
Our first drink in 12 hours!

13:48.550 --> 13:50.340
Help them with the party.

13:48.560 --> 13:50.900
Let's get hammered!

13:50.340 --> 13:53.420
The least you can do is serve us 
after we rescued you.

13:58.820 --> 14:01.150
Chug, chug!

14:01.150 --> 14:03.310
That's it! Don't let him beat you!

14:03.310 --> 14:04.830
More drinks!

14:04.830 --> 14:06.490
We need three more tankards!

14:05.430 --> 14:06.490
I'm empty!

14:06.490 --> 14:07.320
Me, too!

14:08.030 --> 14:11.210
Okay, coming.

14:12.680 --> 14:16.580
So you're the girl Punch found?

14:16.580 --> 14:20.080
Yes. He rescued me.

14:21.510 --> 14:25.590
You sweet thing. Such a cute girl.

14:25.590 --> 14:27.100
Wait, no!

14:30.840 --> 14:31.600
<b>BOOBS</b>

14:31.590 --> 14:33.470
My hands are moving on their own!

14:33.470 --> 14:36.110
I'm old! I can't help it!

14:43.360 --> 14:46.680
Let me know when your cup is empty.

14:47.870 --> 14:50.600
Not bad, girlie!

15:08.310 --> 15:11.330
Are you and your boyfriend fighting?

15:11.330 --> 15:12.910
B-Boy... What?

15:12.910 --> 15:15.510
We're not in that kind of relationship.

15:15.510 --> 15:19.060
If you're not together, then what 
were you two doing out here?

15:19.060 --> 15:21.710
Nah, they must be dating.

15:21.710 --> 15:24.680
After all, she's cute. I'm so jealous.

15:24.680 --> 15:26.430
It's not like that, idiot.

15:26.430 --> 15:32.530
They probably fled here after their country 
was wiped out by Redia, like us.

15:32.810 --> 15:38.010
We're, uh... t-travelers.

15:38.010 --> 15:40.010
Ado...

15:40.010 --> 15:44.940
My friend and I are currently 
traveling the world.

15:44.940 --> 15:47.940
This place is really nice.

15:52.190 --> 15:56.070
This girl is too funny. She's awesome.

15:56.070 --> 15:59.690
Did you hear that? She said 
she's traveling the world.

16:02.080 --> 16:03.700
You're right.

16:07.210 --> 16:09.450
What? Are you all right?

16:14.460 --> 16:17.710
What happened to all of you?

16:18.880 --> 16:24.710
You ended up vagrants because you're not 
careful what you put in your mouths, idiots.

16:24.710 --> 16:27.210
Adonis, what did you do?

16:27.210 --> 16:28.870
Did you poison their drinks?

16:28.870 --> 16:30.150
No.

16:31.010 --> 16:37.470
A few tweaks to alcohol's formula
 turns it into a tranquilizer.

16:37.880 --> 16:40.470
Can't you tell by looking at the formula?

16:41.010 --> 16:42.610
Aren't you supposed to be a witch?

16:42.610 --> 16:43.980
<b>Aren't you 
supposed to 
be a witch?</b>

16:44.180 --> 16:48.590
I-I'm too stupid to understand.

16:48.590 --> 16:51.390
But this means no one's dead, right?

16:51.390 --> 16:52.750
Not yet.

16:53.990 --> 16:55.480
Wait!

16:55.480 --> 16:58.500
Adonis, I think you've got 
the wrong idea about them.

16:58.750 --> 17:01.550
These people have been really kind.

17:01.550 --> 17:06.190
They rescued us from the middle of the 
desert and gave us medicine and bandages.

17:06.190 --> 17:07.570
So, what?

17:08.240 --> 17:10.510
They saved our lives.

17:10.930 --> 17:13.260
Have you heard the expression 
"pardons make offenders"?

17:13.260 --> 17:16.260
If it wasn't for these people, you'd be—

17:17.870 --> 17:19.480
I'm not going to kill them.

17:20.460 --> 17:24.390
Vagrants are subhuman. 
They're not worth killing.

17:26.020 --> 17:27.390
Also...

17:28.970 --> 17:32.790
I've decided I don't need you after all.

17:33.150 --> 17:34.300
Later.

17:35.010 --> 17:38.030
Wait. Why?

17:38.030 --> 17:43.790
Unlike you, I can't laugh 
after losing someone important to me.

17:44.450 --> 17:49.430
I can't imagine joking around 
with people like this.

17:50.740 --> 17:53.940
You and I are fundamentally incompatible.

17:56.150 --> 18:01.700
But what will happen 
if they find out who we are?

18:02.130 --> 18:05.350
We have to blend in with humans.

18:05.350 --> 18:08.700
I can't let them suspect I'm a witch.

18:09.200 --> 18:12.530
So I laugh and keep up appearances.

18:13.950 --> 18:17.720
But I'm obviously not fine 
after what happened to—

18:17.720 --> 18:22.080
If we're not compatible, 
then don't end up like me, Doroka.

18:42.160 --> 18:45.630
Thank you. You're so kind.

18:45.630 --> 18:48.100
Did your boyfriend leave?

18:48.650 --> 18:49.850
Mr. Punch.

18:51.260 --> 18:53.370
He's not my boyfriend.

18:54.440 --> 18:57.550
Either way, he's one brazen guy.

18:57.550 --> 19:00.860
He left without thanking me.

19:01.270 --> 19:05.550
And he left a girl here all on her own?

19:05.550 --> 19:09.120
You were right to break up with him.

19:10.980 --> 19:13.630
No, he...

19:16.430 --> 19:18.390
Don't end up like me.

19:20.270 --> 19:23.220
<i>He's actually very kind.</i>

19:36.490 --> 19:40.400
Revenge won't heal your wounds.

19:40.400 --> 19:43.160
No! Don't do this, Adonis!

19:43.160 --> 19:46.660
What would Chloe think 
if she could see you now?

19:46.660 --> 19:52.660
It was the name the world's greatest 
witch gave to her beloved student.

19:52.660 --> 19:56.930
You're not alone anymore, Adonis.

19:57.850 --> 19:58.820
Damn it.

20:00.430 --> 20:01.980
<i>Pursuers?</i>

20:02.450 --> 20:05.050
<i>Was the tranquilizer too weak?</i>

20:05.450 --> 20:07.360
<i>Or are they from Redia?</i>

20:07.360 --> 20:10.420
<i>No, it doesn't matter.</i>

20:11.290 --> 20:13.620
<i>I'll kill anyone who gets in my way.</i>

20:13.620 --> 20:15.320
<i>Who they are changes nothing.</i>

20:19.550 --> 20:22.450
Adonis the witch's apprentice.

20:22.450 --> 20:24.140
Wh-What did you just say?

20:24.140 --> 20:26.200
That's not him. He's, uh...

20:26.630 --> 20:28.950
He's a completely different man now.

20:29.400 --> 20:30.450
What?

20:30.790 --> 20:33.510
I'll never forget that day.

20:33.990 --> 20:37.260
I saw it as I lay dying.

20:38.970 --> 20:40.420
Glittering snow.

20:41.780 --> 20:43.800
The ice witch.

20:50.210 --> 20:52.610
The greatest happiness a man can know

20:52.610 --> 20:57.070
is having something worth 
fighting against the world for.

20:58.390 --> 20:59.860
Mr. Punch...

21:00.820 --> 21:04.330
Maybe you're right,

21:04.330 --> 21:11.090
but you'll never settle an argument over 
whether or not revenge is wrong.

21:11.490 --> 21:15.720
This world is so relative, 
it makes you want to cover your eyes.

21:17.080 --> 21:19.540
That kid chose revenge.

21:19.540 --> 21:24.710
Even if it leads to his death, 
that's his choice.

21:25.820 --> 21:27.560
What will you do?

21:29.450 --> 21:36.350
I don't want anyone else to die because 
I failed to protect Anna and the others.

21:37.420 --> 21:39.620
So I won't let Adonis die.

21:39.620 --> 21:43.630
Then should you be here 
talking to me, witch?

21:44.110 --> 21:47.580
Move, Adonis!

21:47.580 --> 21:48.480
What?

21:53.860 --> 21:57.120
You idiot! Are you trying to kill me?

21:57.730 --> 22:03.630
Adonis, I'll do my best 
not to get in your way, so...

22:03.630 --> 22:04.700
What?

22:05.690 --> 22:07.840
Let's travel together.

22:10.020 --> 22:14.060
I've thought about it, 
and I think you need me.

22:14.060 --> 22:15.740
Besides, it's dangerous to travel alone.

22:15.740 --> 22:18.500
And they say good company 
makes the road shorter.

22:18.500 --> 22:20.890
I'd get lonely by myself.

22:20.890 --> 22:24.770
Not just me, but both of us.

22:24.770 --> 22:27.690
So I guess you could say 
we should support one another...

22:27.690 --> 22:29.530
Why didn't she stop?

22:33.940 --> 22:37.050
Such a noisy girl.

22:37.540 --> 22:41.550
How do you stop this thing?

22:44.550 --> 22:47.720
You'd better not make her cry...

22:48.300 --> 22:49.940
Help me!

22:49.940 --> 22:51.330
Use the brakes!

22:51.330 --> 22:53.310
It's that thing that looks like a lever!

22:51.800 --> 22:55.330
...Chloe's beloved apprentice.
